    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0227" n="153" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg153"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1809.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1866-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            23, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I enclose herewith a copy of a
                    communication of the 3d instant from John O’Connell, in regard to his brother
                    Thomas, who, it appears, was arrested in Ireland by the British authorities on
                    suspicion of being interested in the Fenian movement, and is now detained in
                    Mount Joy prison, at Dublin. I will thank you to bring the statement of Mr. John
                    O’Connell to the attention of the British government, with a view to the release
                    of his brother, if upon investigation it shall be found that he is innocent of
                    the charges preferred against him.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq.,<hi
                            rendition="#italic"> &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d140-a1.xml" xpointer="d140-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
